W44-A1 butteraugli source-diff audit
2026-05-23 (UTC: 2026-05-24T00:47Z)
Agent: claude-w44-recon-a1

Verdict: RULED OUT — no divergence found that would shift the buttloop's
target metric meaningfully. The Rust butteraugli crate (v0.9.2) is at
parity with libjxl C++ butteraugli at <0.001 relative score (0.1%), and
observed max drift is 0.002% per the CLAUDE.md and the reference_parity
test on 908 cases.

Tests run during audit (release mode, ~/work/butteraugli/butteraugli):
  cargo test --release --test reference_parity   → 4/4 PASS
  cargo test --release --test conformance        → 6/6 PASS, 2 ignored
  cargo test --release --test cross_arch_parity  → 2/2 PASS, 1 ignored

reference_parity covers 908 reference cases captured from libjxl's
butteraugli_main (FIR blur path, recursive Comparator, hardcoded scores).
Tolerance is 0.001 relative; observed max ~2e-5.

Divergence audit table:
  benchmarks/w44_recon_deep_a1_2026-05-23.tsv
  16 rows, ranked by severity. All low/none.

Top-3 highest-EV "fix" candidates (NONE recommended for shipping):
  1. None — every divergence found is at-or-below the 1e-5 score impact
     threshold. Shipping any change would risk regressing the existing
     908-case parity gate.
  2. Document the f64→f32 mask precision compromise (already documented
     in CLAUDE.md "Optimization session 5"); no code change.
  3. If a buttloop wedge cell EVER produces score drift > 0.01 between
     buttloop's internal recon scoring and the post-buttloop final-encode
     scoring, the bug is in the RECONSTRUCTION (not the metric). Per
     W44-138 P-1 candidate: per-iter EPF sharpness recompute. Per W44-111
     candidate: drift_block_map.rs R/G channel residual investigation.

What this audit does NOT prove:
  - It does NOT prove our buttloop targets match libjxl's buttloop. The
    buttloop's target is a function of (a) the metric and (b) what's
    being scored. (a) is at parity per this audit. (b) is the
    reconstruction divergence W44-111 / W44-113 / W44-138 already
    identified as the residual root cause and partially patched via
    W44-105/107/108/109/117/118/120 chain.
  - It does NOT prove libjxl uses our exact code paths internally
    (e.g. archmage vs hwy SIMD dispatch, FIR vs IIR). It proves the
    OUTPUT scores are within 0.002% on 908 reference cases.

